module SeparatorCommentBeforeLambdaItem exposing (..)

-- A `{- c -}` written across a bracket's `,` rides that separator's row before a
-- LAMBDA item, exactly as it does before every other item shape.
--
-- An ITEM continues the line the container already started (`[ ` / `, `), so its
-- flow is an `InlineStart`. A lambda item is the one item shape that arrives
-- wrapped in a `BodyBlock`, and `makePBox`'s generic `BodyBlock` arm hands every
-- caller an `OwnStart` -- under which a leading single-line `{- c -}` is
-- `standaloneLeading`, stands on its own row and drops the item below it. That
-- made the item box multi-line, which broke the whole list open. Rule C3: a
-- comment never forces a break.
--
-- It also cost the author's layout: the flat spelling below and the broken one
-- after it then rendered the SAME bytes, so `fuzzrun.py`'s author-break oracle
-- could no longer see which was written -- 48 of the 49 failures of the
-- 2026-08-20 sweep, all this one shape.
--
-- The fix is the item's `FlowStart`, not the comment's attachment. Keeping the
-- comment out of the `BodyBlock` in `Comments.gren` fixes these three
-- declarations too, and then tears a comment RUN in half: attachment is what a
-- run travels by, so moving one member out while a multi-line sibling stays in
-- reparses differently every pass. The last declaration here is that run, and it
-- oscillated when this was tried the other way.


flatStaysFlat =
    [ 0, {- c -} \q -> q, other ]


-- The same list broken by the author. Both spellings must survive as written;
-- that they collapsed onto one IS the bug.


brokenStaysBroken =
    [ 0
    , {- c -} \q -> q
    , other
    ]


-- THE TWIN that always worked: every other item shape is a bare child of the
-- list, never wrapped in a `BodyBlock`, so its flow was already inline.


plainItemTwin =
    [ 0, {- c -} fn arg, other ]


-- THE BOUNDARY: at the OPENER the comment leads the first item and rides the
-- `[ ` row -- a different slot, and one that already worked.


openerTwin =
    [ {- c -} \q -> q, other ]


-- THE RUN: a single-line comment followed by a multi-line one, in the same `,`
-- gap. Both members stay children of the ITEM, so the run travels whole.


separatorRun =
    [ 0, {- c -} {- second
       row -} \q -> q, other ]
